# Lint and format the staged files, then type check the whole project.
#
# lint-staged is per file, which is what keeps the hook fast. `tsc` has no
# per file mode that still honours tsconfig.json, so the type check is project
# wide and reads the working tree rather than the staged index. A commit made
# with `git add -p` can therefore pass a check that the committed snapshot would
# fail; CI runs the same three commands on the real commit and is the backstop.
pnpm exec lint-staged
pnpm typecheck
